page[41]=new Array("new/Vacancies/admin%20job%20description.htm","PITA","","PITA JOB DESCRIPTION &nbsp; Position: Administrative Assistant Direct Supervisor: Executive Director Job Site: PITA Office – Ramallah Anticipated Start Date: As soon As possible Candidate: ------------ &nbsp; Scope of Work: This is a full time job requires six working days a week from Saturday through Thursday. The incumbent of the post shall hold a B.A. degree in Business administration our equivalents with three years of experience in relevant field, or a diploma with five years of experience. S/He shall have good communication skills, with very good oral and written English. Good computer skills are a must. &nbsp; Specific responsibilities will include but not limited to: 1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Implement all duties related to professionally operate the office including; receiving phone calls, guests and making appointments. Receiving and registering incoming and outgoing mail. Distributing mail as per PITA’s procedures. 2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Assist in the day-to-day operations including drafting routine letters, and sending informative emails. 3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Responsible for filing documents and reports as per implemented procedures. 4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Responsible for the maintenance of office machinery. 5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Administer the in-office stock of stationary and office supplies. 6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Work closely with other coordinators on implementing the planned programs according to the action plan in a timely and professionally manner. 7.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Assist other coordinators in the preparation for the participation in Trade Fairs; study tours and other related marketing and promotional activities as and when required. 8.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Maintain a record of all meeting minutes and report to members of PITA activities. 9.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Help in collecting information and draft periodic newsletter and up-date website. 10.&nbsp; &nbsp;Keep close contacts with members through email shots, faxes, and telephone calls. 11.&nbsp; Keep records of Board meetings, decisions and follow up actions of the Board and committees agendas, diary, procedures and plans. 12.&nbsp; Any other duties as may be required. &nbsp; The incumbent of the post will be evaluated on his performance mainly on team-work and group dynamics, quality of generated documents, ability to communicate with PITA Board, staff and members, in addition to compliance with PITA’s policies and procedures. &nbsp; Please send your CV on or before Thursday 6th September 2001 to: Fax 02 296 4121 Or Email abudaka@pita-palestine.org &nbsp; ");
page[42]=new Array("HR/Workshop%20on%20IT%20HR.htm","Workshop on IT HR","","Workshop on IT HR 23rd May 2001 A presentation by Qais Saleh of MCS and moderated by Sam Bahour and Marwan Tarazi was made to make an initial introduction of the HR IT Framework Study that was recently completed. The main points that were raised and discussed are: No definitions of IT professionals formal qualifications &nbsp; 30% of the Palestinian population are in the school system at any one time, hence adjustment to the education system is most important for greatest impact &nbsp; Palestinian economy lacks the critical mass of IT professionals to have any meaningful IT development. This is a reality that we need to address and not cover with meaningless bean counting. &nbsp; No &quot;pipeline&quot; between public and private sector, thus the education sector was chosen to be the focal point for reform, in order words creating a pipeline that can produce qualified graduates for the market &nbsp; PITA can have input in the development of IT industry in many ways, first step is to put a private sector position paper and instigate policy makers toward the creation of a multi-ministerial commission that would include PITA with the goal of being the central focal point for all levels of education with regards to IT issues, curriculum, facilities, programs, etc. &nbsp; Also PITA can work through technical forums such as the tri-party committee of Education, Higher Education and Labour ministries on vocational training &nbsp; The private (PITA) sector position paper should include &nbsp; Education is a high priority especially in a resistance economy &nbsp; The formation of national body for the formulation and implementation of a national plan on IT and on which the private sector should participate &nbsp; The cooperation of private, public and NGO sectors in short term IT programmes to upgrade graduates. This is not to skip by the current workforce considering the lack of a national strategy or government policy on IT &nbsp; Raising IT awareness and its importance through out the Palestinian society. This will requires the cooperation of all segments of the community &nbsp; Creation of the right environment for IT through the cooperation between government, Educational and training institutions and the private sector &nbsp; Creating a thriving local IT labour pool is to a large degree the government responsibility ");
page[43]=new Array("Straegy/PITA%20Strategic%20Plan.htm","PITA Strategic Plan","","Outline of PITA Strategic Plan &nbsp; Purpose: To represent the collective interest of the private IT sector in Palestine &nbsp; &nbsp; Vision: &nbsp; A: PITA to be recognized as the leader in positioning the IT sector as the economic pillar &nbsp; B: PITA leads the positioning of the IT sector as the economic pillar of Palestine &nbsp; &nbsp; Mission: To promote and defend IT private sector through: &nbsp; ·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Advocating business enabling policies, mechanisms and environment through public-private partnership. ·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Promoting the Palestinian IT sector locally and internationally through facilitating access to markets for the benefit of the PITA members. ·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Engaging the technical and non-technical IT human resources and human resources related institutions in-order to expand qualified pool of which uphold the level of professional standard.  Goals - Objectives - Strategies - Tactics G O S &nbsp; &nbsp; 1 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Advocating business enabling policies, mechanisms and environment through public-private partnership 1 1 &nbsp; &nbsp; Promote the implementation of appropriate policies, laws and regulations, to create a more competitive business environment. 1 1 1 &nbsp; Identify specific priority area to change policies, laws and regulations that result in favorable improvements in business and economic performance. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Commissioning &amp; Publishing Position Papers, Surveys, Studies (local &amp; regional) §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Awareness Campaigns on specific issues that are affecting the business environment 1 2 &nbsp; &nbsp; Promote the adoption of public-private national forum(s) and mechanisms for Dialogue 1 2 1 &nbsp; To Partner with stake-holders to build alliances &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Joint Reception, conferences co-sponsorship, media events, §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Assist local education institutions in co-op training opportunities, job fairs &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Goals - Objectives - Strategies - Tactics G O S &nbsp; &nbsp; 2 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Promoting the Palestinian IT sector locally and internationally through facilitating access to markets for the benefit of PITA members. 2 1 &nbsp; &nbsp; Assist its members to deliver competitive services &amp; products to enable market access 2 1 1 &nbsp; To promote the adoption of international best practices in business &amp; management &nbsp; §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Awareness Seminars, Workshops, Study Tours §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Training §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Recognition 2 2 &nbsp; &nbsp; Expand the market share in target markets through market entry strategy for competitive products and services 2 2 1 &nbsp; Identifying target markets &nbsp; §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Market Intelligence (studies, surveys, correspondents) §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Alliances with sister organizations 2 2 2 &nbsp; Promoting the Palestinian IT products and services in target markets and marketing channels &nbsp; §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Assist companies to participate in relevant international events to better understand market requirements in order to design and produce a competitive marketed products and services §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Assist clusters of companies to conduct market research to better understand target markets §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Note: Put performance indicators §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Spread awareness about the use and benefits of IT applications in other sectors (to increase demand) Goals - Objectives - Strategies - Tactics G O S &nbsp; &nbsp; 3 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Engaging the technical and non-technical IT human resources and human resources related institutions in-order to expand qualified pool of which uphold the level of professional standard. 3 1 &nbsp; &nbsp; Increase the number of quality IT professionals 3 1 1 &nbsp; Promote Quality Institutions/Departments/Centers &nbsp; §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Co-sponsorship of events §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Recognition §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Input of course design 3 1 2 &nbsp; Promote IT disciplines &nbsp; §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Awareness at Schools, Public 3 1 3 &nbsp; Promote IT education in non-IT disciplines &amp; School education &nbsp; §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Awareness at Schools, Public, departments, donations, sample programs §&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Annual IT Show &nbsp; ");
page[44]=new Array("Gitex2001/GITEX2001_PR1_Launch_Final.htm","Palestine to Participate at Gitex 2001 - Dubai","","&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE 05 June, 2001 &nbsp; Contact Information: Mashhour Abudaka, Ph.D., DIC. Executive Director PITA PO Box 2460, Ramallah, Palestine Tel: 970-2-296-1988 Fax: 970-2-296-4121 abudaka@pita-palestine.org &nbsp; &nbsp; Palestinian IT Firms Mobilized for GITEX 2001 &nbsp; &nbsp; Ramallah, Palestine – The Palestinian Information Technology Association for Companies (PITA) announced today its sponsorship of the Palestinian Pavilion @ GITEX 2001.&nbsp; GITEX 2001 is the premier Middle East IT trade exposition to be held October 14-18 this year in Dubai.&nbsp; PITA’s presence at GITEX will highlight the notable growth and momentum of the Palestinian IT sector, and showcase the various new IT business opportunities in Palestine for the international investor. &nbsp; PITA’s Chairman, Ibrahim Barham, states, “A defining characteristic of the IT industry worldwide, and particularly here in Palestine, is its ability to look beyond current realities and to chart a course towards the future.&nbsp; As one of Palestine’s pioneer industry trade associations, PITA represents Palestinian firms from every corner of the IT spectrum.&nbsp;&nbsp; Our members understand the critical importance of establishing external market linkages at this crossroads of development.&nbsp; GITEX 2001 will provide our members direct access to new markets, while at the same time opening doors for international firms willing to explore the many possibilities of Palestine.&nbsp; No other Palestinian economic sector is as uniquely poised for growth as information technology.&nbsp; At GITEX, Palestine’s IT sector will firmly establish itself as one of the international IT community’s new business arenas.” &nbsp; The Palestinian Pavilion @ GITEX 2001 will highlight a number of bold new infrastructure, human resource and technology initiatives currently underway in Palestine. &nbsp; GITEX is the largest and most successful event of its kind in the Middle East and &nbsp;it has firmly established itself as the premier exhibition for computing and communication systems and applications dedicated to the IT industry and the entire business environment. &nbsp; PITA is a membership-based private sector organization representing IT companies in Palestine. It was established in 1998, and is registered with the Palestinian Ministry of Economy &amp; Trade. PITA’s membership comprises software, hardware, systems integrators, telecommunication, office equipment and consulting companies. Its headquarters is located in Ramallah, Palestine.&nbsp; Contact PITA by telephone at 970-2-296-1988, by fax at 970-2-296-4121 or by email at info@pita-palestine.org. &nbsp; &nbsp; Mr. Ibrahim Barham, Chairman of PITA, is available for follow-up interviews.&nbsp; Contact him via telephone at 970 2 296-1988 (PITA) or by e-mail at info@pita-palestine.org &nbsp; &nbsp; # # # &nbsp; ");
page[45]=new Array("Gitex2001/GITEX2001_PR2_Firms_Final.htm","Palestinian Companies at Gitex 2001 - Dubai","","FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE &nbsp; 26 June, 2001 &nbsp; Contact Information: Mashhour Abudaka, Ph.D., DIC. Executive Director PITA PO Box 2460, Ramallah, Palestine Tel: 970-2-296-1988 Fax: 970-2-296-4121 abudaka@pita-palestine.org &nbsp; Palestinian IT Firms Mobilized for GITEX 2001 &nbsp; Ramallah, Palestine - The Palestinian Information Technology Association for Companies (PITA) will sponsor the Palestinian Pavilion @ GITEX 2001 (at Hall 8). PITA’s presence at GITEX will highlight the notable growth and momentum of the Palestinian IT sector, and showcase the vast number of new IT business opportunities in Palestine for the international investor.&nbsp; The following members of PITA will be exhibit at GITEX 2001 (alphabetically): &nbsp; Arab Technology System (www.ats-pal.com) Founded in 1994, ATS is the largest software house in Palestine, with a strong presence in the public and private sectors.&nbsp; Principal products/services include: Oracle Applications (Financial), Jdeveloper, JFP, Designer, ORACLE-8i.&nbsp; ATS is an Oracle certified VAD, Oracle Approved Education Center, a CISCO Reseller, and Novell Business Partner.&nbsp; ATS will exhibit a Municipality Management System; University Admission &amp; Registration System; Archiving System (DACS); Health Care System; Human Resources Management System; Billing System and ERP System. Contact: Hassan Kassem, President &amp; CEO, ph: 970-2-298-7011, info@ats-pal.com &nbsp; ASAL Technologies (www.asaltech.com) Founded in 2000, ASAL Tecnologies is a promising software outsourcing company offering its services to international hi-tech companies.&nbsp; Its full line of products and services include: software outsourcing and development services; Professional and technical software consultation; Custom software application development; Quality assurance, testing and coding; and Internet, programming solutions &amp; localization.&nbsp; ASAL offers the benefit of a highly qualified team of professionals, with an emphasis on quality and timliness.&nbsp; Contact: Abdallah Salameh, Business Development Manager, ph: 970-2-240-9101, asalameh@asaltech.com &nbsp; Babil Soft (www.Babil.com) Founded in 1992, Babil Soft provides top-notch financial management solutions for small and medium size enterprises, through IT consultancy and software development and applications.&nbsp; Babil will exhibit and promote its products and services including: SHAM Financial Management System; SHAM Non-Profit Financial Management Sytem; SHAM Rent-a-Car System; SHAM Service After Sale; and SHAM Payroll System.&nbsp; Contact: Muhana A. Manasra, Manager, ph: 970-2-240-3791, bblsft@jrol.com &nbsp; Bisan Systems Ltd (www.bisan.com) Founded in 1988, Bisan is a software development specializing in object oriented and Java programming. Bisan is well known for its BISAN Accounting and Management system, and will showcase at GITEX its new Enterprise Financial &amp; Management System. Contact: Marwan Totah, CEO, ph: 970-2-298-5941, totah@bisan.com &nbsp; ModernTech&nbsp; (www.mtcgaza.com) Established in 1994, ModernTech Corp. is a leader company in the field of Software development with various products like Accounting System, Employees Management System, Medical &amp; Patients System, University Registration System, Hotel Management System, Kids Educational &amp; Entertainment programs. MTC is experienced in introducing the total solution of training, maintenance, networking &amp; Internet distribution.&nbsp; Contact:&nbsp; Rassem Mushtaha&nbsp;, General Manager, ph: 970-8- 282-4099, mtcg@mtcgaza.com &nbsp; Noursoft (www.noursoft.com) Established in 1996, Noursoft is an IT consultancy and software development company, custom producing software for medium and large businesses.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Noursoft will exhibit: a Library Information System; Document Management System; Educational Institution Management System; and Secured Municipality Billing System.&nbsp; Contact:&nbsp; Omar Said Ismail, General Manager, ph: 970-2-240-5756, noursoft@p-ol.com &nbsp; Palestinian Internet Services Co., Ltd (P-I-S) (www.p-i-s.com) Established in 1998, the Palestinian Internet Services Co., Ltd (P-I-S) is an Internet/Intranet service and solution provider.&nbsp; The company specializes in web site design and hosting, custom Linux applications, domain name registration and Internet connectivity.&nbsp; P-I-S’s strength comes from its diverse and talented staff of engineers, IT and data professionals. Contact: Ahmed Abumarzouq, President &amp; CEO, ph: 970-8-284-3197, info@p-I-s.com &nbsp; PCNC 2000 Networking Ltd (www.pcnc2000.com) PCNC 2000 Networking Ltd primarly develops and implements electronic transaction software and hardware.&nbsp; PCNC 2000’s main products and services it will exhibit include:&nbsp; Credit/Debit Card Processing programs and equipment; Networking Equipment; and Communication Protocol Development and Programs. Contact: Iyad K. Qumsieh, General Manager, ph: 972-2-274-7503, iqumsieh@pcnc2000.com &nbsp; Sidata Information and Communication Systems Ltd. (www.sidata.net) Sidata is a Palestinian provider of a complete range of top-quality IT related solutions, including custom software development for clients.&nbsp; Sidata’s main products and services include: software development and outsourcing services, professional and technical software consultation, custom software application development, quality assurance, testing and coding, and Internet and programming solutions.&nbsp; Contact: Bassem El Wazir, Managing Director, ph: 970 -8-282-5131, belwazir@hally.net &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; More information on exhibiting companies can also be found at PITA's website (www.pita-palestine.org). &nbsp; &nbsp; GITEX is the largest and most successful event of its kind in the Middle East and it has firmly established itself as the premier exhibition for computing and communication systems and applications dedicated to the IT industry and the entire business environment. PITA is a membership-based private sector organization representing IT companies in Palestine. It was established in 1998, and is registered with the Palestinian Ministry of Economy &amp; Trade.&nbsp; PITA’s membership comprises software, hardware, systems integrators, telecommunication, office equipment and consulting companies. Its headquarters is located in Ramallah, Palestine.&nbsp; Contact PITA by telephone at 970-2-296-1988 , by fax at 970-2-296-4121 or by email at info@pita-palestine.org # # # ");
page[46]=new Array("Gitex2001/PR(04Oct01)-PalestineIT%20Sector%20Set%20for%20Take-off.htm","Press Release","","&nbsp; Press Release Palestinian IT Sector Set To Take Off &nbsp; On October 14-18th the Palestinian IT sector will make it’s debut with a national pavilion at the GITEX 2001 international IT exhibition in Dubai. 04 October 2001 &nbsp; &nbsp; Seven Palestinian IT companies, together with representatives of PITA the Palestinian IT Association of companies, Paltrade the Palestinian Trade Center, and a public relations team will take part in the GITEX 2001 exhibition, which is the largest and most successful event of its kind in the Middle East, attracting tens of thousands of visitors from around 100 countries. GITEX 2001 is the first time that Palestine has had a country Pavilion at such an exhibition, and marks an exciting step forward for the Palestinian IT sector, as it looks toward regional and international markets and partners.&nbsp; &nbsp; Industry sources note that the IT sector in Palestine has been growing at a rate of 25-30% annually from 1998.&nbsp; Dr. Samir Abdullah, General Director of Paltrade says that “despite the restrictions facing the development of the Palestinian economy, the IT sector has attracted significant investment, and this momentum has been maintained during the last year of intifada as companies continue to invest, train staff and grow”.&nbsp; With the delegation to this year’s GITEX, Palestinian IT companies are now looking to expand their presence regionally and internationally.&nbsp; &nbsp; “As a result of international involvement in Palestine, diaspora connections and the many Palestinians who complete higher education overseas, as well as Palestine’s geographical location, we are uniquely placed to be an IT bridge between east and west” points out Dr. Mashhour Abudaka, Executive Director of PITA.&nbsp; With a recent study from Killen &amp; Associates indicating IT spending in the Middle East growing at twice the world average and expected to top US$46 billion in 2002, there couldn’t be a better time to start building that bridge. &nbsp; Information Technology in Palestine represents not only a viable business opportunity but is also a prime example of Palestinian creativity and determination in the face of restrictions and limitations imposed by Israel’s ongoing occupation.&nbsp; Palestine offers many stories of IT conquering physical and political barriers: internet cafes overcoming isolation for Palestinian young people; the ‘Across Borders’ project linking refugees scattered around the world; and the use of video conferencing allowing families locked in by closure to participate in the university graduation ceremonies of their sons and daughters, and the Palestinian Authority to hold Legislative Council meetings despite Members being unable to travel between West Bank and Gaza.&nbsp; The increasingly widespread and creative use of IT in Palestine both indicates the growing importance of the sector and strengthens its continuing development. &nbsp; Andersen (previously Arthur Andersen) is the main sponsor of the Palestinian delegation to GITEX 2001, with the Islamic Development Bank the main supporter, through the Al-Aqsa Fund for Palestine.&nbsp; The delegation is also supported by Dubai Internet City and the Dubai World Trade Center, as evidence of Arab support and interest in the Palestinian IT sector. &nbsp; The seven companies set to exhibit at GITEX include Palestine’s largest software house and its only Oracle VAD &amp; Education Partner, and offer a range of innovative software and services.&nbsp; The exhibitors will be seeking resellers and distributors for custom-designed software, as well as looking to make contacts for future outsourcing work.&nbsp; Some of the exhibitors are already serving international clients from the Middle East and Europe, while for others the exhibition is their first move into these markets. &nbsp; The organized private sector, in concert with governmental commitment to and donor support for IT sector development, indicate that the IT sector is likely to continue its impressive rate of growth in the coming years.&nbsp; Palestine led the Arab world in privatizing it’s telecommunications network, leading to the $65 million investment that has resulted in a new, state-of-the-art, 100% digital infrastructure.&nbsp; Governmental commitment has been manifested in a large-scale overhaul of the educational curricula at all levels of schooling to include a greater IT and English-language component, new investment-friendly laws and the formation this week of a committee bringing together ministerial and private sector representatives to investigate strategies for IT-related human resources development.&nbsp; IT has also been identified as a focus for development support by several of the major donors providing aid to Palestine, ensuring the future capital and technical resources for development. &nbsp; In light of the shock waves sent out around the world by the recent events in America, GITEX 2001 is a particularly important event for the Palestinian delegation, demonstrating not only the level of development reached by the industry, but also the reality of the educated, internationally conversant Palestinian population, working for and investing in the future despite the odds.&nbsp; The sector is looking forward to an exciting exhibition. &nbsp; For more information on GITEX exhibitors, and IT sector facts and figures contact: Amanda Scothern, Consultant, Ellam Tam for Communications &amp; Public Relations Ph: +970/2 2 2409105/7, mobile: +97/2 59 789 781, in Dubai (10-19 Oct): +971 50 585 9942 e-mail: amanda@ellamtam.com &nbsp; GITEX website: www.gitex.com &nbsp; Contact for comment: Dr. Mashhour Abudaka (Executive Director, PITA) Ph: +970/2 59 695883, at GITEX, Dubai: +971 50 585 9788 e-mail: abudaka@pita-palestine.org Dr. Samir Abdullah (General Director, Paltrade) Ph: +970/2 2 59 580 789, e-mail: sabdullah@paltrade.org Omar Sahili (PITA Advisor &amp; IT Sector Manager, DAI Inc.) Ph: +970/2 50 460 387, at GITEX, Dubai: +971 50 585 9798 e-mail: Omar_Sahili@dai.com &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Anderson, Main Sponsor &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Islamic Development Bank, Main Supporter &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ");
page[47]=new Array("Gitex2001/PR(14Oct01)2Sheikhs%20at%20GITEX%20opening.htm","Press Release","","14 October 2001 Press Release Crown Prince Sheikh Mohamed and Minister of Finance and Industry Sheikh Hamdan visit Palestinian Pavillion Opening at GITEX 2001 &nbsp; &nbsp; Sheikh Mohamed Ben Rashid Al Maktoum, Crown Prince and Minister of Defence of UAE, and Sheikh Hamdan Ben Rashid Al Maktoum, Deputy Ruler of Dubai and UAE Minister of Finance and Industry, both visited the Palestinian Pavilion on the occasion of the opening at GITEX 2001.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; They were greeted at the Pavilion by H.E. Mr. Maher Masri, Palestinian Minister of Trade who was visiting Dubai as the head of the Palestinian Delegation to GITEX 2001.&nbsp; H.E. Minister Masri welcomed both Sheikhs as they arrived at the Pavilion and presented them with gifts on behalf of the Palestinian Delegation, in appreciation of UAE’s support and goodwill toward Palestine.&nbsp; &nbsp; Sheikh Mohammed said that he considered the Palestinian Participation very important and he assured the Palestinian Delegation that the focus on development of the Information and Communications Technology (ICT) is the way to the future. &nbsp; Sheikh Hamdan, UAE Minister of Finance, expressed his pleasure at the Palestinian Participation for the first time in GITEX, and wished good luck and success to the Delegation. &nbsp; Mr Ibrahim Barham, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Palestinian IT Association of companies (PITA), briefed Sheikh Mohamed and Sheikh Hamdan about the Palestinian participation in GITEX 2001 and the significant progress of development of the IT sector in Palestine during the last years, in spite of a difficult situation. &nbsp; GITEX 2001 marks the first time Palestine is participating as a national delegation in such an exhibition.&nbsp; The Palestinian delegation includes seven IT companies, showcasing a range of products and services, and is coordinated by sector representative PITA, as well as Paltrade (Palestine Trade Center).&nbsp; The event is expected to open new business opportunities for Palestinian companies, and to increase awareness of the potential of the developing Palestinian IT sector.&nbsp; &nbsp; The Main Sponsor for the Palestinian participation is Andersen (previously Arthur Andersen) and the Islamic Bank is the Main Supporter through it’s Al-Aqsa Fund for Palestine.&nbsp; The Pavilion is also supported by Dubai Internet City (DIC) and the Dubai World Trade Center (DWTC), as evidence of Arab support and interest in the Palestinian IT sector. &nbsp; Following the exciting opening to GITEX 2001 this morning, the Palestinian Pavilion looks forward to a busy exhibition and to developing increased contacts and partnerships in the region and internationally. &nbsp; For more information on GITEX exhibitors, and IT sector facts and figures contact: Amanda Scothern, Consultant, Ellam Tam for Communications &amp; Public Relations Ph: +970/2 2 2409105/7, mobile: +97/2 59 789 781, in Dubai (10-19 Oct): +971 50 585 9942 e-mail: amanda@ellamtam.com &nbsp; &nbsp; Contact for comment: Dr. Mashhour Abudaka (Executive Director, PITA) Ph: +971 50 585 9788&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; e-mail: abudaka@pita-palestine.org Dr. Samir Abdullah (General Director, Paltrade) e-mail: sabdullah@paltrade.org Omar Sahili (PITA Advisor &amp; IT Sector Manager, DAI Inc.) Ph: +971 50 585 9798&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; e-mail: Omar_Sahili@dai.com &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Andersen, Main Sponsor &nbsp; Islamic Development Bank, Main Supporter &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ");
page[48]=new Array("Gitex2001/PR(16Oct01)BusinessNotCharity.htm","Press Release","","16 October 2001 &nbsp; &nbsp; Press Release &nbsp; Palestinian Minister of Trade: “We are looking for business partners, not charity” &nbsp; H.E. Maher Al-Masri, Palestinian Minister of Trade, assured the audience at a dinner reception held by the Palestinian Delegation to GITEX 2001, that the Palestinian IT private sector is looking for mutually beneficial business cooperation with Arab and other partners, not for charity aid.&nbsp; He added that the Palestinian IT sector is now ready for this kind of partnership, despite the current hardships faced by the Palestinian people. &nbsp; He said that even after a year of intifada, the business sector is still producing, especially in the IT sector.&nbsp; “After the development of the telecommunications infrastructure, an essential foundation for the development of the IT sector, that has taken place in the last few years, we are looking forward to real investment and partnership with the Arab world, because we are confident that exciting business opportunities exist in Palestine, particularly given the independence of IT from borders and physical restrictions”. &nbsp; He assured the audience of the full support of the Palestinian Authority (PA) for the IT sector, manifested in the creation of laws and regulations supporting the development of the sector, including a new law on Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) to be approved.&nbsp; He said that “the PA puts IT as first priority since it is seen to be one of the sectors key to future Palestinian development”.&nbsp;&nbsp; The Minister noted that the Ministry of Trade had formed a committee to follow up the issue of IPR and the PA have made many efforts to improve the IT sector in various other areas, including education.&nbsp; He pointed out that the sector has experienced a high growth rate since the establishment of the PA in Palestine, particularly in recent years, with 25-30% annual growth from 1998.&nbsp; &nbsp; The Dinner Reception at which the Minister spoke was attended by the Palestinian Consul in Dubai, Saleem Abu Sultan, and a number of guests from the Arab world and elsewhere.&nbsp; &nbsp; Andersen (previously Arthur Andersen) was honoured with a gift at the dinner as the main partner of the Palestinian participation in GITEX 2001.&nbsp; The Islamic Development Bank was also honoured with a gift in appreciation of its support as main supporter, through the Al-Aqsa Fund for Palestine.&nbsp; The speakers expressed appreciation to DWTC and DIC for their support of the Palestinian Delegation to GITEX Dubai 2001. &nbsp; The reception included a presentation by Mr. Omar Sahili, IT expert from Palestine on the IT sector and its possibilities for potential investors and business partners.&nbsp; Mr. Sahili discussed Palestine IT’s “People and Potential”, detailing what is offered in the areas of Human Resources, infrastructure, legal environment and financial services, and education. &nbsp; For more information on GITEX exhibitors, and IT sector facts and figures, and to arrange interviews, please contact: Amanda Scothern or Amjad Malki, Palestinian Delegation Press Team Ph in Dubai (10-19 Oct): +971 (0)50 585 9942,&nbsp; (Ph in Palestine: +970/2 2 2409105/7) e-mail: amanda@ellamtam.com, malki@ellamtam.com &nbsp; GITEX website: www.gitex.com &nbsp; Contact for comment: Dr. Mashhour Abudaka (Executive Director, PITA) Ph:at GITEX, Dubai: +971 50 585 9788&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; e-mail: abudaka@pita-palestine.org Dr. Samir Abdullah (General Director, Paltrade) e-mail: sabdullah@paltrade.org Omar Sahili (PITA Advisor &amp; IT Sector Manager, DAI Inc.) Ph at GITEX, Dubai: +971 50 585 9798&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; e-mail: Omar_Sahili@dai.com &nbsp; ");
page[49]=new Array("Gitex2001/PR(16Oct01)Palestine-DIC%20(Gergawi)%20Mtg.htm","Press Release","","16 October 2001 &nbsp; &nbsp; Press Release &nbsp; Dubai Internet City (DIC) Director General, Mohammad Gergawi and Palestinian delegation agree on Palestine@DIC office. &nbsp; Mohammad Gergawi, Director General of DIC, meeting this morning with Mr. Ibrahim Barham and Dr. Mashhour Abudaka of PITA. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Mr. Mohammed Abdulla Al Gergawi, Director General of Dubai Internet City (DIC) met today with Mr. Ibrahim Barham, Chairman of the Board of the Palestinian IT Association, and others representing the IT sector in Palestine, at the DIC Pavilion at GITEX 2001 to talk about a planned office for Palestine at DIC. &nbsp; The meeting resulted in an agreement in principle to launch a Palestinian office at DIC, to be called Palestine@DIC.&nbsp; More meetings are expected to finalise the details of a Memorandum of Understanding between the two parties. &nbsp; Mr. Gergawi told the Palestinians to “consider us as partners” and also expressed his belief that IT is key for the future strength of the Palestinian nation.&nbsp; Mr. Ibrahim Barham discussed the growing IT sector in Palestine, pointing out to Mr. Gergawi the governmental support for IT development, in addition to the organised and dynamic private sector.&nbsp; He said that the Palestinian IT sector considers this year’s participation in GITEX to be the first step toward International markets, and that the planned presence at DIC will be key in expanding into Arab markets and developing business partnerships in the region.&nbsp; Mr. Barham also said that the Palestinian sector views DIC and the IT industry in Dubai as role models for future Palestinian development. &nbsp; Seven Palestinian IT companies are exhibiting at the Palestinian Pavilion at GITEX 2001 at stand 820.&nbsp; The companies are showcasing a range of products and services.&nbsp; 28 custom-designed software products are on exhibit, for a range of applications including banking &amp; finance, accounting, education administration and educational software, internet-related applications, health and tourism systems, and human resources management. &nbsp; The exhibiting companies include the leading software and outsourcing companies in Palestine.&nbsp; They expect their participation in GITEX 2001 to provide further contacts with potential outsourcing clients and business partners.&nbsp; In addition, the companies are demonstrating a range of Arabised software products aimed at regional markets. &nbsp; Visit the Palestinian Pavilion at Stand 820, Hall 8. For more information on exhibiting companies, contact details below. &nbsp; For more information on GITEX exhibitors, and IT sector facts and figures, and to arrange interviews, please contact: Amanda Scothern or Amjad Malki, Palestinian Delegation Press Team Ph in Dubai (10-19 Oct): +971 (0)50 585 9942,&nbsp; (Ph in Palestine: +970/2 2 2409105/7) e-mail: amanda@ellamtam.com, malki@ellamtam.com &nbsp; Contact for comment: Dr. Mashhour Abudaka (Executive Director, PITA) Ph:at GITEX, Dubai: +971 50 585 9788&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; e-mail: abudaka@pita-palestine.org Dr. Samir Abdullah (General Director, Paltrade) e-mail: sabdullah@paltrade.org Omar Sahili (PITA Advisor &amp; IT Sector Manager, DAI Inc.) Ph at GITEX, Dubai: +971 50 585 9798&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; e-mail: Omar_Sahili@dai.com &nbsp; ");
page[50]=new Array("Gitex2001/Sponsorships/Sponsorship_PackageFinal_Explained.htm","Draft for discussion","","THE PALESTINIAN PAVILION  @ GITEX 2001 Dubai 14 - 18 October, 2001 SPONSORSHIP AND ADVERTISING The Palestine Information Technology Association (PITA) in cooperation with the Palestine Trade Center (Paltrade), under the auspices of the Ministry of Economy and Trade with the support of the DAI-MAP project is mounting the Palestinian Pavilion at GITEX 2001 in Dubai, UAE from 14-18 October 2001. &nbsp; CITEX is the largest and most visible IT exhibition in the Middle East. Due to its incremental success GITEX has been ranked the third most important IT exhibition in the World. &nbsp; PITA sees the exhibition as the right vehicle at the right time to launch its market entry into the regional Arab Markets and benefit from the networking opportunities with the international IT Sector representatives expected to be present at GITEX 2001. &nbsp; PITA in a continuing effort to create a professional image for the sector and assit exhibitors to both exhibit their own procucts plus showcasing the Palestinian IT Sector Milestones, has recruited the assitance of PALTRADE, the specilaized Trade Promotion Center in Palestine, and Ellam Tam, the Communications and Public Relations Company in Palestine. &nbsp; In order for PITA to ensure an efficient and proactive presence at GITEX with a longer term aim for networking, PITA is looking for valuable assistance with sponsorship and advertising. An attractive range of options has been prepared that offers both exposure and recognition for your companies in an international forum of recognized significance.   PITA is eager to receive your support and assistance to this crucial mission in GITEX 2001. &nbsp; Sponsorship Packages &nbsp; Gold Sponsorship Packages: &nbsp; I.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Palestine GITEX Main Partner: &nbsp; The Main Partner in return for his sponsorship will receive a wide host of recognition rights including. These rights will include: -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Designation of Main Partner at the Palestinian Pavilion main Banner -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Designation of Main Partner at the front Cover of the Catalogue -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Designation of Main Partner on the front Cover of the Brochure -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Designation of Main Partner on the front of the Calendar if sponsored. -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Designation of Main Partner on all IT sector Press Releases -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Designation of Main Partner on Acknowledgement page inside Catalogue -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Designation of Main Partner on Roll up Banner in meeting room at Pavilion -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Exclusive hosting of the Palestinian Reception with name/logo appearing on Banner for event and invitation cards -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Speaking opportunities at reception and press conference. -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 10 executives at Reception and ability to invite up to 20 guests from AA’s contacts -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Full page ad in Catalogue &nbsp; The Palestine GITEX Main Partner has been awarded to Arthur Andersen Company in the Middle East at a total package cost of USD$ 50,000. &nbsp; II.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Palestine GITEX Associate Partner: &nbsp; The Associate Partner in return for his sponsorship will receive the following recognition benefits: &nbsp; -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name appearance on Main Banner at Pavilion -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name appearance front cover of Catalogue -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name appearance on Brochure -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name appearance on Calendar -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name appearance in acknowledgement page inside Catalogue -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name appearance on Roll up Banner in meeting room at Pavilion -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Acknowledgement at Reception -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Ability to invite 15 guests to the Palestinian reception -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Exlcusive name appearance as sponsor for the fully paid ad at Newsweek Magazine Middle East Edition -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Designation as Associate Partner appearing at Press Releases. &nbsp; Designation of Associate Partner is open any Palestinian or international company or organization. The total Package cost is at USD$ 30,000. &nbsp; III. Palestine GITEX Supporter: &nbsp; The desingation of Palestine GITEX Supporter is open for three Palestinian/International Companies or entities who are willing to ensure the appropriate presentation of the Palestine IT Sector at GITEX 2001. The three supporters in return for their sponsorship will receive the following recognition benefits: &nbsp; -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name appearance on Main Banner at Pavilion -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name appearance on front cover of Catalogue -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name appearance on Brochure -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name appearance on Calendar -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name appearance in acknowledgement page inside Catalogue -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name appearance on Roll up Banner in meeting room at Pavilion -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Acknowledgement at Reception -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Ability to invite 10 guests to the Palestinian reception -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Exlcusive name appearance on Carrier Bags for first Supporter -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Exclusive name appearance on IT Brochure for second Supporter -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Exclusive name appearance on Calendar for third Supporter -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Designation as Associate Partner appearing at Press Releases. &nbsp; Designation of Supporter Partner is open any Palestinian or international company or organization. The package is estimated at USD$ 15,000. &nbsp; Silver Sponsorship Packages: &nbsp; IV.&nbsp; Exhibition Catalogue for the Palestinian Pavilion &nbsp; The print run will be 5000 copies and the catalogue will be distributed free to all visitors. It will contain details of exhibitors and other useful information about Palestine. It will include two support letters from  Palestinian Ministers. Your name will be prominently displayed on the front cover of the catalogue along with the words: This catalogue has been sponsored by [Name and address] &nbsp; The Sponsor of the Exhibition Catalogue will get the opportunity to receive the following benefits: &nbsp; -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Display company name on front cover of the catalogue along with the words: This catalogue has been sponsored by [ Name and Adress] -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A full page ad inside the catalogue free of charge. -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Ability to attend or  invite 3 guests to AA’s reception. -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Recognition in the friends list banner at meeting room. &nbsp; &nbsp; An exhibition catalogue has a much longer life that the exhibition itself. It is retained by visitors both as a reminder and as a reference for future use.  Your name will be the first thing they see every time it is opened. &nbsp; Exhibition catalogue sponsorship is open toThe cost of sole-sponsorship of the catalogue (and a permanent reminder of your company) is $10,000. As only one sponsor is being used, this sponsorship is available on a first-come-first-served basis. &nbsp; Please complete the attached pro-forma and forward it as soon as possible. The deadline for exhibition catalogue sponsorship is 19th September. &nbsp; V.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Full Paid Ad in Newsweek Magazine Middle East Edition: &nbsp; For the first time, sponsors can have the exclusivity of sponosring a full page in the Middle East edition of Newsweek Magazine profiling the Palestinian IT Sector and the Palestinian Economy. The Middle East Edition of Newsweek has a 11,000 circulation with a signigicant  readership. &nbsp; The Sponsor can benefit the following: -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Company Brand name appearing as the main Sponsor for the advertisement page.. -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Full page ad in the catalogue free -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Appearance on back cover of the Catalogue as Designated Friend of Palestine CITEX 2001 -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Appearance at a special roll up banner at the meeting room at the Palestinian Pavilion. &nbsp; Additionally the Sponsorship package will also include the distribution of an additional 500 copies of the magazine at the Palestinian Pavilion, the Palestinian Reception, and the planned press conferences. &nbsp; Exhibition catalogue sponsorship is open toThe cost of sole-sponsorship of the one page ad is $10,000. As only one sponsor is being used, this sponsorship is available on a first-come-first-served basis. &nbsp; Please complete the attached pro-forma and forward it as soon as possible. The deadline for exhibition catalogue sponsorship is 19th September. &nbsp; VI.&nbsp; Palestinian IT Profile Brochure: &nbsp; The print run will be 1,000 copies of a first class IT Sector Profile to be distributed free to all visitors. It will contain a profile of the sector, its players, the existing conditions and the future growth opportunities for the sector. Sponsor will benefit from the following: &nbsp; -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name will be prominently displayed on the front cover of the Brochure along with the words: This Brochure has been sponsored by [Name and address]. -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Opportunity to place a quarter page profile of your company inside the Brochure in a special designated area or to be aknowledge at the catalogue as designated friend -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Appearance at a special roll up banner at the meeting room at the Palestinian Pavilion as Designated Friend of Palestine CITEX 2001. &nbsp; An IT Sector Profile Brochure has a much longer life that the exhibition itself. It is retained by visitors both as a reminder and as a reference for future use.  Your name will be the first thing they see every time it is opened. &nbsp; IT Sector Profile Brochure sponsorship is open toThe cost of sole-sponsorship of the Brochure (and a permanent reminder of your company) is $5,000. As only one sponsor is being used, this sponsorship is available on a first-come-first-served basis. &nbsp; Please complete the attached pro-forma and forward it as soon as possible. The deadline for exhibition catalogue sponsorship is 19th September. &nbsp; VII.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Carrier bags &nbsp; You could be the sole sponsor of the Palestinian Pavilion Carrier Bags. The production run will be 1000 pieces. The bag is made of sturdy cotton fabric, will hold folders brochures and other items visitors will accumulate during the exhibition, and will be distributed free. Sponsor will benefit the following: -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name will be prominently displayed on both sides of the bag. (so that whichever way it is held your name will appear). Each bag will carry the words: Palestinian Pavilion GITEX 2001 and This carrier has been provided by [Name and address]. -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Appearance on back cover of the Catalogue as Designated Friend of Palestine CITEX 2001 -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Appearance at a special roll up banner at the meeting room at the Palestinian Pavilion. &nbsp; Customized text can also be considered provided sponsorship agreement is received in good time to allow production. &nbsp; An exhibition carrier has a much longer life that the exhibition itself. It is both a reminder and useful.  Your name will be seen every time it is used. &nbsp; Exhibition carrier sponsorship is open to any Palestinian or international company or organization. The cost of sole-sponsorship of the carrier bags (and a continuing reminder of your company) is $5,000. As only one sponsor is being used, this sponsorship is available on a first-come-first-served basis. &nbsp; Please complete the attached pro-forma and forward it as soon as possible. The deadline for carrier bag sponsorship is 19th September &nbsp; VIII.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Travel Package: &nbsp; An essential package designed to enable the effective and encompassing presence of the IT Sector Delegations and other key support staff. &nbsp; The sponsor of the Travel Package will benefit the following: &nbsp; -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Sepcial acknolwedgement at the reception. -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Appearance on back cover of the Catalogues as official carrier of Palestinian deligation at CITEX 2001 -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Appearance at a special roll up banner at the meeting room at the Palestinian Pavilion as official carrier &nbsp; Travel Package sponsorship is open to any Gulf/Arab or international Carriers or Travel Agency. The cost of sole-sponsorship of the Travel Package is $5,000. As only one sponsor is being used, this sponsorship is available on a first-come-first-served basis. &nbsp; Please complete the attached pro-forma and forward it as soon as possible. The deadline for carrier bag sponsorship is 19th September &nbsp; IX.&nbsp;  Calendar 2002: &nbsp; A special Calendar for 2002 will be printed on the occasion of the Palestine GITEX 2001 participation. &nbsp; &nbsp; The Calendar will be designed as a desktop give away and will be distributed (2000) Calendar to all visitors of the Pavilion, reception guests and VIPs. Sponsor will be able to get the following: &nbsp; -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  Name will be prominently displayed on top of Calendar. Each calendar will carry     the words: Palestinian Pavilion GITEX 2001 and This Calender has been provided  by [Name and address]. -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Appearance on back cover of the Catalogue as Designated Friend of Palestine CITEX 2001 -    Appearance on a special roll up banner at the meeting room in the Palestinian                                                                         Pavillion. Calendar 2002 sponsorship is open to any Palestinian Company. The cost of sole-sponsorship of the Calendar 2002 is $5,000. As only one sponsor is being used, this sponsorship is available on a first-come-first-served basis. &nbsp; Please complete the attached pro-forma and forward it as soon as possible. The deadline for carrier bag sponsorship is 19th September &nbsp; X.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Palestine GITEX Friend: &nbsp; Sponsors who still wish to be general supporters of the Palestinian Presence at GITEX 2001 are still welcome to do so. In return they will benefit the following: &nbsp; -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Appearance on back cover of the Catalogue as Designated Friend of Palestine CITEX 2001 -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Appearance at a special roll up banner at the meeting room at the Palestinian Pavilion. &nbsp; Friend of Palestine GITEX 2001 Designation is open to six Palestinian/Gulf/Arab or international Companies. The cost of thePalestine GITEX  Friend Designation is $1,500. &nbsp; Please complete the attached pro-forma and forward it as soon as possible. The deadline for carrier bag sponsorship is 19th September &nbsp; Advertising Packages &nbsp; Besides sponsorship you may also wish to consider advertising to support your involvement in the exhibition. This can be done in the exhibition catalogue. &nbsp; Exhibition Catalogue for Palestinian Pavilion &nbsp; The catalogue will be in full color with a print run of 3,000 copies. It will contain details of exhibitors and other useful information about Palestine. It will include two support letters from  Palestinian Ministers. It will be distributed free to all visitors. &nbsp; An exhibition catalogue has a much longer life that the exhibition itself. It is retained by visitors both as a reminder and as a reference for future use.  Your advertisement will be seen every time it is opened. &nbsp; Exhibition catalogue advertising is open to any Palestinian or international company or organization. &nbsp; The cost of advertising is as follows: &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Back cover, full page only,                                 $4,000 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Inside front cover, full page only,                        $3,000 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Inside back cover, full page only                         $3,000 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Full page, alongside company profile if possible                                                            $1,200 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Half page, alongside company profile if possible                                                              $700 &nbsp; A discount of 25% is offered on the above rates to sponsors, exhibitors, members of PITA,  and members of Paltrade. &nbsp; Please complete the attached pro-forma and forward it as soon as possible to book advertising space. As the number of advertisements is limited, bookings will be accepted on a first-come-first-served basis. The deadline for advertising in the exhibition catalogue is 19th September. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Thank you once again for your support. &nbsp; &nbsp; Palestine Information Technology Association                    Palestine Trade Center &nbsp; 2nd of September 2001 &nbsp; Attached: Proforma ");
page[51]=new Array("Gitex2001/Sponsorships/Gitex01_SponsorshipAd_Package_listOnly.htm","Fax Form / MAP","","SPONSORSHIP AND ADVERTISING (Deadline: 19 Sep 2001) &nbsp; A. Gold Sponsorship Packages No Item Price Slots Name of Sponsor A-1 Palestine GITEX Main Partner $50,000 One Arthur Andersen A-2 Palestine GITEX Associate Partner $30,000 One &nbsp; A-3 Palestine GITEX Supporter $15,000 Three &nbsp; &nbsp; B. Silver Sponsorship Packages No Item Price Slots Name of Sponsor B-1 Exhibition Catalogue $10,000 One &nbsp; B-2 Reception $10,000 One Arthur Andersen B-3 Full Paid Add in Intl IT Magazines $10,000 One &nbsp; B-5 Carrier bags $5,000 One &nbsp; B-6 Palestinian IT Profile Brochure $5,000 One &nbsp; B-7 Travel Package $5,000 One &nbsp; B-8 Calendar 2002 $2,500 One &nbsp; B-9 Palestine GITEX Friend $1,500 Six &nbsp; &nbsp; C. Advertising Packages (At the Exhibition Catalogue) No Item Cost Sponsors Name of Advertiser C-1 Back cover, full page only. $4,000 One Only &nbsp; C-2 Inside front cover, full page only. $3,000 One Only &nbsp; C-3 Inside back cover, full page only. $3,000 One Only &nbsp; C-4 Full page, alongside company profile if possible. $1,200 &nbsp; &nbsp; C-5 Half page, alongside company profile if possible. $700 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;     Notes for Item C: -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A discount of 25% is offered to sponsors, exhibitors, members of PITA, and members of Paltrade. -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The Electronic Files of the advertisements are to be submitted by the deadline to Paltrade. &nbsp; Date: &nbsp; Total: US (                   ) &nbsp; Name: &nbsp; &nbsp; Company: &nbsp; Signature: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; You Have Been Contacted By: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Signed Forms &amp; Ad materials are to be sent to Paltrade (Attn: Mr. Majed Nazzal) at Fax: 2 295 9449 or mnazzal@paltrade.org by no later than 15 Sep 2001 For queries and information Contact Ellam Tam at: Acknowledgments: Special Thanks to the Islamic Development Bank &amp; Dubai Internet City For their valuable Support &nbsp; Tel: 970 2 2409105/7, Fax: 970 2 8409107, Email: info@ellamtam.com ");
page[52]=new Array("BusDev/Year2001/Qlty_Sys_Assess_Dev/Qlty_syst_Assess_Dev_ProgAnnounce.htm","Internationl Quality Systems: Assessment &amp; System Development","","Market Access Program Firm Level Assistance International Quality Systems for IT Companies Program: International Quality Systems for IT Companies: Assessment &amp; Systems Development 5 Time Frame: July 2001 - Apr 2002 Program Summary: PITA and Market Access Program (MAP) would like to announce this Firm Level Assistance Program aiming to help companies improve their business management and products /services in compliance with international standards. This program comes as a follow-up to the &quot;International Quality Systems for IT Companies&quot; workshop; hence, priority will be given to companies that participated in the workshop. Tracks: A.&#9;Assessment &amp; Report: A thorough assessment / audit to be made to each company against ISO 9001: 2000 or CMM resulting in a detailed Audit Report (Management, Marketing, Procedures, Admin, etc.) of company status, recommendations and estimated level of effort needed to improve systems. This report is intended to be used as a guideline for each company whether it chooses to continue for next development phases of not. The audit will be made according to international standards framework. Note:&#9;Based on the results of the assessment reports, a customized &quot;Partial System Development&quot; Technical Assistance and Training programs will be designed as a follow-up. OR B. System Development: Companies ready to go for a full system development against ISO 9001:2000 or CMM should register for this track. Companies in this track would have an audit report done (same as above) and also implementation of recommendations. This track should qualify companies for certification*. * &#9;This program does not cover the cost of third party international certification. Target Group: 10 ICT Companies for Track &quot;A&quot; 3 ICT companies for Track &quot;B&quot; The Service Providers: Track &quot;A&quot; will be executed by MAP contractors. Track &quot;B&quot;: Service providers are selected based on a tender jointly done with MAP for each company. Cost: Track &quot;A&quot;: Registration fees are $500 paid directly to PITA. Non-members' fees are $650. Track &quot;B&quot;: Registration fees are $500 paid directly to PITA. In addition, MAP will subsidize (reimburse) 40% of the total cost of system development and up to $4,000. For non-members, MAP would subsidize (reimburse) 20% and up to $2,000. Partial system development depends on the level of effort and the number of days needed as estimated in the Audit Report. To Apply: Attached Application Form should be filled &amp; emailed to PITA at (pita@pita-palestine.org). Advanced payment of $500 with the submission of the Application. Company Profile filled at PITA website and for MAP. Additional for Track &quot;B&quot;: Attended the mentioned workshop A letter of expression on how this program would benefit the company A Letter of Agreement signed with MAP FIRST COME FIRST SERVE For more information, please contact Omar Al-Sahili, 02 298 7187. ");
page[53]=new Array("BusDev/Year2001/Qlty_Sys_Assess_Dev/Qlty_syst_Assess_Dev_RegistForm.htm","Internationl Quality Systems: Registration Form","","Market Access Program Firm Level Assistance International Quality Systems for IT Companies Registration Form &nbsp; 5 Company name: &nbsp; &nbsp; Main Business: &nbsp; &nbsp; Established Since: &nbsp; Representative: &nbsp; Title: &nbsp; Address: &nbsp; &nbsp; City: &nbsp; &nbsp; E-mail: &nbsp; Tel: &nbsp; Fax: &nbsp; Interest: &nbsp; Track &quot;A&quot; Assessment &amp; Report Track &quot;B&quot; System Development ISO 9001 : 2000 &nbsp; &nbsp; CMM &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Signature: Please return this form to PITA by 2 Aug 2001 by email to pita@pita-palestine.org - Subject: International Quality Systems: Assessment &amp; Systems Development. ");
page[54]=new Array("BusDev/Year2001/Gitex01Prep/Description/Gitex2001_CompanyTA_ProgAnnounce.htm","GITEX Firm Level Assistance","","&nbsp; Program: Assisting Companies to prepare for exhibition at Gitex 2001 Time Frame: July 01 Program Summary: This program is part of an overall Firm Level Assistance Program that's implemented by PITA &amp; DAI/MAP. This particular program is to prepare exhibiting at GITEX in terms of&nbsp; Planning, Image Building, and Media &amp; Market Info. An Independent consultant will be hired to implement part of the task on cost sharing basis. His / Her work will be evaluated as days of Level of Effort. &nbsp; Details: Planning: Working with the company team to plan for Gitex (Goals, Theme, Products, Image Building, Media, Marketing Needs, etc.) Image Building: Website content, Promotional Material, Adds, etc. Media: Press Releases, Interviews Market Info: Identification of individual company market needs (Meetings, Contacts, Prospects, etc.) &nbsp; Deliverables: 1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Company plan and scope of follow-up needs 2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Material of image building and press releases &nbsp; Process: 1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Assessment of company needs based on a short company visit 2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Workplan &amp; budget to define Level of Effort needed 3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Letter of Agreement signed with DAI /MAP 4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Implementation Target Group: -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Companies exhibiting at Gitex 2001 Cost: MAP will subsidize up to 50% of the cost of the consultant and the design of the printed material for the purpose of GITEX. All company dues are paid directly to PITA. To Apply: -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Attached Application Form should be emailed it to PITA at (pita@pita-palestine.org). -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Advanced payment of $200 with the submission of the application. -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Your Company Profile should be filled at PITA website and for MAP. &nbsp; Note: &nbsp; Based on the output of this program, implementation of follow-up activities needed (e.g. Meetings, Market research, etc.) will be handled separately. Back ");
page[55]=new Array("BusDev/Year2001/Gitex01Prep/Forms/Gitex2001_CompanyTA_RegistForm.htm","GITEX Firm Level Assistance Registration Form","","Registration Form &nbsp; Company name: &nbsp; &nbsp; Main Business: &nbsp; &nbsp; Established Since: &nbsp; Representative: &nbsp; Title: &nbsp; Address: &nbsp; &nbsp; City: &nbsp; &nbsp; E-mail: &nbsp; Tel: &nbsp; Fax: &nbsp; &nbsp; Please return this form to PITA by 3 July 2001 by email to pita@pita-palestine.org - Subject: Gitex 2001 - Firm Level Assistance. &nbsp; Needs Assessment Meeting Time Requested: (Tentative) &nbsp; DAY Morning Midday Afternoon 1. &nbsp; Wed, 4 July 01 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 2. &nbsp; Thu, 5 July 01 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Back ");
page[56]=new Array("BusDev/Year2001/FinAdvice/Description/FinancialAdvise_CompAssess_ProgAnnounce.htm","Financial Advice Program","","Program: Company Assessment &amp; Advice on Financial Structure &amp; Performance Time Frame: 4th Week of May 01 &amp; 1st Week of June 01 Program Summary: The program includes a one or two day company assessment to revise and discuss the financials structure, performance and planning (all or any) for each participating company. It's required that the decision makers of each interested company to be engaged in this program. Program Tracks: 1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Assessing the current financial structure, performance &amp; planning (al or any) and suggest improvements Prerequisites: 3 Years track of company financials 2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Assisting in Structuring the Financials Prerequisites: Knowledge of Business Planning and attendance of the Business Planning Course offered by PITA &nbsp; Deliverables: Report &amp; Recommendations Process: 1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Application forms recived &amp; screened 2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; An introductory visit to assess needs (1-2 hours) 3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; TA as described above (1-2 days) &nbsp; Target Group: -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Companies that have business plans and plan to expand;&nbsp; -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Companies that have business plans and interested in assessing/re-structuring their financials The Conultant(s): John Landsburg, Consultant, MAP. Mr. Landsburg is a company assessment specialist how has over 35 years of experience in the areas of banking &amp; financial assessment. Mr. Omar Al-Sahili, the IT Sector Manager at MAP will accompany Mr. Landsburg in his company visits. Criteria: -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; PITA members -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; First Come First Serve in addition to screening Fees: $100 per day (Paid to PITA) To Apply: -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Attached Application Form should be emailed it to PITA at (register@pita-palestine.org). -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Full Payment -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Company Profile filled at PITA website &nbsp; Back ");
page[57]=new Array("BusDev/Year2001/FinAdvice/Forms/FinancialAdvise_CompAssess_RegistForm.htm","Financial Advice Program Registration Form","","Registration Form &nbsp; Company name: &nbsp; &nbsp; Main Business: &nbsp; &nbsp; Established Since: &nbsp; Representative: &nbsp; Title: &nbsp; Address: &nbsp; &nbsp; City: &nbsp; &nbsp; E-mail: &nbsp; Tel: &nbsp; Fax: &nbsp; Fees: PITA Member:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; $ 100 Per company per day &nbsp; Please return this form to PITA by 27 May 2001 by email to register@pita-palestine.org - Subject: Financial Advice. &nbsp; Company Meeting Time Requested: (Tentative) &nbsp; DAY Morning Midday Afternoon 1. &nbsp; Tue, 29 May - 01 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 2. &nbsp; Wed 30 May 01 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 3. &nbsp; Thu, 31 May 01 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Back ");
page[58]=new Array("BusDev/Year2001/QltySystems/International%20Quality%20Systems%20fo%20IT.htm","International Quality Systems fo IT Companies","","PITA SERVICES 2001 Quality Systems Workshop 27 Jan 2001 &nbsp;Dear Valuable Member; As part of its services for the year 2001 and in association with DAI/MAP, PITA is proud to announce the WORKSHOP: &quot;International Quality Systems for IT Companies&quot; Objectives of Workshop: 1.&#9;Introduce participating IT companies to different quality management systems standards and models 2.&#9;Guide the companies to the quality system that best suits their needs 3.&#9;Introduce a follow-up program with interested companies to execute a Gap Analysis against selected standards Day: Saturday, 27 Jan 2001 Time: 8:30 AM Place: Grand Park (tentative, to be confirmed for registrant), Ramallah Audience: Top Management Cost [Material Included]: PITA Members: &#9;&#9;Free Non-PITA Members:&#9;$ 50 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Please fill the attached registration form and return it to PITA not latter that 12:00 HR Wednesday 24/01/2001 at Fax: 02-296-4121 &nbsp; &nbsp; Note: A similar workshop will be held in Gaza as soon as logistics are arranged. &nbsp; International Quality Systems for IT Companies Program &nbsp; Session Title Topics Time Speaker &nbsp; Registration &nbsp; 8:30 - 9:00 &nbsp; &nbsp; Welcome Speech §&#9;PITA Service Plan 9 - 9:10 Ibrahim Barham &nbsp; MAP Prospective &nbsp; 9:10 - 9:20 DAI 1.&#9; Software Process Improvement -SPI §&#9;Intro to Quality Systems §&#9;Benefits of SPI 9:20 - 10:20 Dr. Amjad Al-Ghanim &nbsp; Break &nbsp; 20 min &nbsp; 2.&#9; Capability Maturity Model-CMM §&#9;Introduction to the CMM 10: 40 - 11:55 Dr. Amjad Al-Ghanim &nbsp; Break &nbsp; 25 min Snacks 3.&#9; ISO 9001: 2000 §&#9;Emphasis of the new version of the system standards 12:20 - 1:20 Dr. Amjad Al-Ghanim 4.&#9; Software Life Cycle Processes: - ISO/IEC 12207:1995 §&#9;Major components of the Standard and benefits 1:20 - 2:20 Dr. Amjad Al-Ghanim &nbsp; Break &nbsp; 20 min &nbsp; 5.&#9; Too many Standards/Models?? §&#9;How to choose 2:40- 3:10 Dr. Amjad Al-Ghanim 6.&#9; Follow-up Program §&#9;Next Step: The Gap Analysis 3:10 - 3:20 Omar Al-Sahili &nbsp; Closing &nbsp; 3:20 Ibrahim Barham Registration Form Company name: &nbsp; &nbsp; Main Business: &nbsp; &nbsp; # of Employees: &nbsp; Participant: &nbsp; &nbsp; Title: &nbsp; Address: &nbsp; &nbsp; City: &nbsp; &nbsp; E-mail: &nbsp; Tel: &nbsp; &nbsp; Fax: &nbsp; Fees: Member:&#9;&#9;$ 0 Non-Member:&#9;$ 50 Per person &amp; including material Please fill this form and return to PITA no later than 12:00 HR Wednesday 24/01/2001 at the No. Fax: 02-296-4121. Seats are limited. ");
page[59]=new Array("BusDev/Year2001/BusPlan/business_planning_training_cours.htm","Business Planning Training Course","","PITA SERVICES 2001 Business Planning Training Course 11 &amp; 13 Jan, 2001 &nbsp; Dear Valuable Member; As part of its services for year 2001, PITA announces the Business Planning training courses: &quot;Designing Roadmaps for Success&quot; The overall goal is to support the Palestinian ICT sector by helping companies to address key business challenges. The training course will address the need and fundamentals of Business Planning with in-depth concentration on Financial &amp; Marketing Management. The course will have case studies and also the option to have a per-company private consultation with the consultant. The company may choose take advantage of the private meeting in any way. The course will be delivered by PITA in association with DAI over a two-day period. Dates: Thu 11 Jan 2001 &amp; Sat 13 Jan 2001 Time: 9 Am to 4 PM Place: Al-Bireh Municipality Audience: Top Management Cost [Material Included]: PITA Members: &#9;&#9;$80 per person Non-PITA Members:&#9;$140 per person &nbsp; Main Lecturer: Dr. Bernard O'Sullivan: Bernard O' Sullivan has worked on business planning and analysis in Europe, Asia and the Middle East. In Asia he worked for HSBC and Bank of China as well as various venture capitalist funds. Recently he has been working in Palestine examining investment and joint venture opportunities on behalf of European companies. Program DAY 1&#9;&#9;Thursday 11 Jan 2001 &nbsp; Session Title Time Speaker &nbsp; Welcome Speech 9:30 - 9:40 Ibrahim Barham 1.&#9; Session 1: &#9;Introduction to Business Planning 9:40 - 10:40 Bernard O'Sullivan &nbsp; Break 20 min Dr. Coffee 2.&#9; Session 2:&#9;Business Planning Format 11:00 - 12:30 Bernard O'Sullivan &nbsp; Follow-up Program 12:30 - 12:45 Omar Al-Sahili &nbsp; Break 30 min Dr. Snacks 3.&#9; An Example / Discussion 1:15 - 2:30 Bernard O'Sullivan 4.&#9; The Home Work!! 2:30 - 3:15 Bernard O'Sullivan DAY 2&#9;&#9;Saturday 13 Jan 2001 5.&#9; Session 3: &#9;&quot;MARKETING&quot; in the Business Plan 9:30 - 11:00 Bernard O'Sullivan &nbsp; Break 20 min Dr. Coffee 6.&#9; Session 4: &#9;&quot;FINANCIALS&quot; in the Business Plan 11:20 - 12:40 Bernard O'Sullivan 7.&#9; Using the WEB for Business Planning! 12:40 - 1:00 Bernard O'Sullivan &nbsp; Closing Remarks 1:00 - 1:10 Said Abu Hijleh &nbsp; Closing 1:10 Ibrahim Barham Registration Form Company name: &nbsp; &nbsp; Main Business: &nbsp; &nbsp; Established Since: &nbsp; Representative: &nbsp; &nbsp; Title: &nbsp; Address: &nbsp; &nbsp; City: &nbsp; &nbsp; E-mail: &nbsp; Tel: &nbsp; &nbsp; Fax: &nbsp; Fees: Member:&#9;&#9;$ 80 Non-Member:&#9;$ 140 Per person &amp; including material Private meeting with consultant requested (2-3 Hours) Yes &#9;/ &#9;No Please return this form to PITA by 10 Jan 2001 at Fax 02-296-4121. Seats are limited. Company Private Meeting Time Requested: (Tentative) DAY Morning Midday Afternoon Sun 14 Jan &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Mon 15 Jan &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Tue 16 Jan &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Wed 17 Jan &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ");
